      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T13:28:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Whether to wrap it in a module should be configurable.\n\nFor library variants this adds an additional level of hierarchy that seems unnecessary, e.g.\n\n   my_proto_crate_name::my_proto_mod_wrapper::\n\nMy thoughts are we shouldn\u0027t pass this flag when generating the code for library variants, but then it also means that our library variants are generating different source which doesn\u0027t seem great either.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8ffa160_3d6deab0",
        "filename": "rust/protobuf.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T21:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have been back-and-forth on this choice.\nI think the trouble of additional layer can be reduced into one extra \"use declaration\" in user code to introduce a short alias. As you said, applying wrap_in_module\u003d\u003csource_stem\u003e gives consistent module name to the generated code, no matter it is included, imported, or linked.\n\nAnother design choice is to make \"source_stem\" optional and not to wrap-in-module without source_stem. Or we can make that choice later when there are more use cases.",
      "parentUuid": "ce976df9_fbf9c058",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45a096c3_b3ad3a16",
        "filename": "rust/protobuf.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T22:01:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that when root_module is true, it should perhaps even be an error to add a module wrapping name. If we are putting it in a crate already, it already has a name, and doesn\u0027t need another name underneath.",
      "parentUuid": "e8ffa160_3d6deab0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1caed1a7_c0721507",
        "filename": "rust/protobuf.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-01T00:53:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A valid use case to enable both wrap_in_module and root_module is to \"include\" the generated file into one rust module, and also build a library with the generated file in a library. This would happen in aosp/1414179 when codegen_only:true is not set but lib.rs \"include\" generated .rs file.\n\nIt is more consistent that each .proto file is compiled into one Rust module, with the same wrap_in_module name, and that module can be include into another rust module like the cdisk_spec_proto module or the protos module in crosvm. In this case the module name is cdisk_spec.\n\nWhen the generated code is imported implicitly from the file cdisk_spec.rs, with the default protobuf-codegen flags and no wrap_in_module, the imported module is also called cdisk_spec.",
      "parentUuid": "45a096c3_b3ad3a16",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f83e5a1d_656482ec",
        "filename": "rust/protobuf.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T13:28:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s make this configurable with a property in ProtobufProperties, which defaults to this value.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d4ac7c2_fe8c9d37",
        "filename": "rust/protobuf.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T21:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At line 68, i saw that we use getStem(ctx) used for the output .rs file base name.\nShouldn\u0027t we just reuse source_stem property as the user configurable module name?\nIt\u0027s Rust convention to import/include modules from files with the same name.",
      "parentUuid": "f83e5a1d_656482ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c430c33_6a662329",
        "filename": "rust/source_provider.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T12:50:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a case where we\u0027d want to explicitly not provide a library variant of a module? The library variant is only built if something pulls it in as a library dependency.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71d35376_fac7e0d9",
        "filename": "rust/source_provider.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T13:28:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I\u0027d like to avoid adding this property unless there\u0027s a use case. Under normal circumstances we want to encourage using generated code as libraries. There might be cases where there is a need to \u0027include\u0027 them, but this is already possible without this flag.",
      "parentUuid": "9c430c33_6a662329",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1d8521c_b317d940",
        "filename": "rust/source_provider.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T21:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In aosp/1414179 I set codegen_only:false to avoid unused cdisk_spec_proto libraries. Without it the unused *proto libraries are still generated. Now the generated cdisk_spec.rs is included into libprotos as crosvm used to do. When crosvm enables more features and include more generated .rs files and it does not need more separate *proto libraries.",
      "parentUuid": "71d35376_fac7e0d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9f60c7a_d05776c1",
        "filename": "rust/source_provider.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T22:01:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These libraries should only be built in checkbuilds or if used. If they\u0027re being built when the source code is included but the library is not used, that\u0027s a separate bug, and not one we should be solving by disabling the feature.",
      "parentUuid": "e1d8521c_b317d940",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c63de92_e1f94d3a",
        "filename": "rust/source_provider.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
